{"name":"Akari Red","hex":"#c90b42","fetched":"2026-10-20","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the colour which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive colour.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Akari (space telescope)","blocks":[{"text":"AKARI (ASTRO-F) was an infrared space telescope developed by Japan Aerospace Exploration Agency (JAXA), in cooperation with institutes of Europe and Korea. It was launched on 21 February 2006, at 21:28 UTC by M-V rocket into Earth Sun-synchronous orbit. After its launch it was named AKARI (明かり), which means light in Japanese. Earlier on, the project was known as IRIS."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/ASTRO-F_%27AKARI%27_illust.jpg/330px-ASTRO-F_%27AKARI%27_illust.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akari_(space_telescope)","wikidata":"Q298047"},{"title":"Akari (wrestler)","blocks":[{"text":"Bemita Elgueta Saldias, better known by her ring name Akari, is a Chilean professional wrestler currently performing in the Japanese promotion Pure-J where she is a former Princess of Pro-Wrestling Champion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/20230516akari.jpg/330px-20230516akari.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akari_(wrestler)","wikidata":"Q111111941"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/ASTRO-F_%27AKARI%27_illust.jpg/500px-ASTRO-F_%27AKARI%27_illust.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/ASTRO-F_%27AKARI%27_illust.jpg/1280px-ASTRO-F_%27AKARI%27_illust.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/ASTRO-F_%27AKARI%27_illust.jpg/500px-ASTRO-F_%27AKARI%27_illust.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AASTRO-F_'AKARI'_illust.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/20230516akari.jpg/500px-20230516akari.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/20230516akari.jpg/1280px-20230516akari.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/20230516akari.jpg/500px-20230516akari.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A20230516akari.jpg"},{"srcset":"http